WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.436
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:05.237
This is the show to be at!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:06.639
This is the show to watch!

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.975
Thank you for being here.
Let's get to some news.

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:12.978
Well, guys, tensions are high
between Russia and Ukraine,

00:00:12.978 --> 00:00:15.749
so President Biden just had
a call with Vladimir Putin,

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.784
and he invited him
to meet in person.

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:21.887
And when they first meet, Putin
will hand Biden a box and say,

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:24.323
"These are some of Donald's
things he left at my place.

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:26.192
Can you give to him?

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.661
Thank you."

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:32.532
Yep, Biden asked Putin to meet
in a neutral third country.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:33.600
Because meeting up with Putin

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.335
is like buying something
off Craigslist.

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:36.569
You want to meet in
a public place,

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:37.736
where everyone can see you.

00:00:37.736 --> 00:00:41.007
It's like, "Beanie Babies first,
cash second.

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:44.310
You know the way this works.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.111
You show me
Mr. Peanut the Elephant,

00:00:46.111 --> 00:00:48.848
and I show you the cash."

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.183
But you can never trust Putin.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.918
He started the call by saying,
"Joe, give me

00:00:52.918 --> 00:00:57.690
Social Security number
so I know it's really you."

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.126
Yep, during the call,
Biden was pretty tough on Putin

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:02.962
over Russia's aggressive actions
towards Ukraine.

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:05.865
Putin was like,
"Ugh, this freakin' guy.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:08.233
He's like the poison
in my underpants.

00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:11.137
Hello? Keep talking."

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.538
You could tell Biden
was being tough, though,

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:14.307
because Putin's translator
kept saying,

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:17.209
"Oh, please don't make me
tell him that.

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:20.647
Remember, Vlad,
I'm just a translator."

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.482
And today, The White House
said their goal

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:24.817
is to have a
"predictable relationship"

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.218
with Russia.

00:01:26.218 --> 00:01:28.287
I mean, it's
already pretty predictable.

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:29.622
Every four years,
we have an election,

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.725
and every four years,
they try to hack it.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:33.926
But the president is busy.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:35.528
It was just announced that
Biden will deliver

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:38.564
his first address to a
joint session of Congress

00:01:38.564 --> 00:01:40.066
two weeks from today.

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:42.802
Yeah, it will be the first time
in four years Nancy Pelosi

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.204
will sit behind a president

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:46.806
and not want to bang
the gavel on his head.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.076
Yep, Biden will deliver
the official address.

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:52.311
Then trump will crash
a Mar-a-Lago wedding

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:54.280
to give his rebuttal.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.650
And this is big.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.252
Today, Biden made
an important announcement

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.519
about the war in Afghanistan.

00:02:00.519 --> 00:02:01.854
Listen to this.

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:04.657
-After consulting closely
with our allies and partners,

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.925
with our military leaders
and intelligence personnel,

00:02:06.925 --> 00:02:10.563
with our diplomats
and our development experts,

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.565
with the Congress
and the vice president,

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:16.736
I concluded that it's time to
end America's longest war.

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:19.004
It's time for
American troops to come home.

00:02:19.004 --> 00:02:20.406
-During his remarks,

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:23.176
Biden announced that withdrawal
would begin on May 1st.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.344
And then, when the troops get
home, they're gonna be like,

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:27.580
"Why are all the bars closed?"

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:32.685
[ Applause ]
What's going on?"

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:38.224
Get this -- Egypt has
seized the giant ship

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.760
that blocked the Suez Canal.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.928
And they're not letting it go
until the owners pay

00:02:42.928 --> 00:02:45.698
$900 million in damages.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:46.899
You know what?

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:48.935
That story was so
much fun for the whole world.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:52.604
I'm sure we can get a GoFundMe
going to pay off the tab, right?

00:02:53.105 --> 00:02:54.807
You can tell the ship
needs money fast

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:57.376
because, today,
it started an OnlyFans.

00:02:57.376 --> 00:02:59.812
-Oh.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.849
All hands on deck.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.250
-All hands on what?
-Deck.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.854
-Okay, yeah.

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:11.056
-Wow!

00:03:11.056 --> 00:03:13.559
-It's been a rough couple of
weeks for that captain.

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:14.861
Today, he was eating Pringles

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.629
and then got his hand
stuck in the can.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:19.098
"Oh, you've got to be
kidding me!"

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.568
Well, this isn't good
for those of you

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:23.936
trying to grill this summer.

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:24.937
Check this out.

00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:26.105
-Experts are predicting

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:29.108
a possible pork shortage
this summer.

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:31.677
They say as restaurants reopen

00:03:31.677 --> 00:03:34.380
and people start having
more social gatherings,

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.682
pork products,
like hot dogs and bacon,

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:38.251
may be hard to
come by this summer.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.986
-What?! Oh, man!

00:03:40.986 --> 00:03:42.021
I was really looking forward to

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:44.323
grilling up some swine
this summer.

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:46.391
-Yeah. Sorry about that, Tariq.

00:03:46.391 --> 00:03:47.693
-It's all good.

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:51.764
Well, at least I can still enjoy
my favorite summer drink,

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:54.300
a nice refreshing boba tea.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.469
-Oh.

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:58.504
-"Oh" what?

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.006
-Roll the clip.

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.874
-Running out of the boba tea

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:05.177
was behind a nationwide shortage
of tapioca pearls.

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:07.913
-What?!

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:11.250
No pork or boba tea?!

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.385
Well, at least I can still plan

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:14.386
to relax in my pool
over the summer.

00:04:14.386 --> 00:04:16.422
-Well...

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:18.090
-Don't say it.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.658
-Roll the clip.

00:04:19.658 --> 00:04:20.859
-For those of you planning to

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:22.394
relax in your pool
over the summer,

00:04:22.394 --> 00:04:24.764
it could be in jeopardy due to
a chlorine shortage.

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.665
-Oh, come on!

00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:27.700
-I mean, I'm sorry, Tariq.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.801
I'm sure you'll
find something fun

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.770
to pass the time this summer.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:33.272
-Yeah, I guess so.

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:34.873
Maybe I'll buy a boat.

00:04:34.873 --> 00:04:37.743
-Looking to buy a boat, perhaps?
You may be out of luck.

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:40.513
Recent events leading to
a boat shortage.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:43.682
-Maybe I'll look to buy
a new house

00:04:43.682 --> 00:04:45.685
or do a
home-improvement project.

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:47.352
-If you're looking to
buy a new house

00:04:47.352 --> 00:04:50.623
or do a home-improvement
project, you'll be paying more.

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:54.126
A lumber shortage has
caused prices to skyrocket.

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:56.929
-Maybe I'll eat ketchup packets

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:59.298
at some of the
biggest restaurant chains.

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:01.700
-There's apparently a
ketchup-package shortage,

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.870
and it's hitting some of
the biggest restaurant chains.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.838
-I give up.

00:05:06.838 --> 00:05:08.608
This summer is a bust!

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.643
-Oh, hey, come on, come on.
Look on the bright side.

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:12.678
You're scheduled to get
your first vaccine.

00:05:12.678 --> 00:05:13.946
-That's true.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.447
-Which one are you
going to get, again?

00:05:15.447 --> 00:05:16.949
-Johnson &amp; Johnson.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:21.353
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:23.456
-Let's just move on.
Let's move on.

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:25.491
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.095 --> 00:05:32.999
Get this -- there's a
new custom-made Ford Bronco

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:35.334
going on sale for $400,000.

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:37.270
Take a look at this thing.
-Whoa!

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:38.471
-Wow!

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:41.174
MotorTrend says
its in-class towing can haul

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:44.643
even the most fragile male egos.

00:05:44.643 --> 00:05:47.880
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.482
[ Imitates engine revving ]

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:51.216
Okay, alright, alright.

00:05:51.216 --> 00:05:54.720
-"It's got a horn!"

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.322
-I read about a couple
over in England

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:58.657
who ripped up an old carpet
in their house and found

00:05:58.657 --> 00:06:00.492
a life-sized Monopoly board
underneath.

00:06:00.492 --> 00:06:01.493
Take a look at this thing.

00:06:01.493 --> 00:06:04.696
Isn't that cool? Yeah.

00:06:04.696 --> 00:06:06.599
If you get mad during a game
on that Monopoly board,

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:09.268
you have to flip over
the entire house.

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:14.774
Unfortunately, the couple
can't leave the room

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:15.808
until they finish the game.

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:20.680
It's the British version
of "Jumanji."

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.281
The previous owners
must have been pretty wild,

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:23.949
because when they pulled up
the carpet in the bedroom,

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:25.418
they found a giant
"Twister" board.

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:27.186
-Really?
-I'm just sayin', man.

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:30.156
-Ooh-la-la!
♪♪

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:33.492
-Some more important news
from the U.K.

00:06:33.492 --> 00:06:36.896
Darius, the world's longest
rabbit, is missing.

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:38.831
-Oh.
-He weighs 50 pounds.

00:06:38.831 --> 00:06:39.832
Here he is.

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:41.567
-Ooh!

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:42.868
-Yeah. Wow.

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:45.304
Well, they've put up
some missing posters for him.

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:46.806
Check it out. This one says...

00:06:52.177 --> 00:06:53.746
This next one says...

00:06:56.548 --> 00:06:59.786
Up next, this one says...

00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:05.191
-[ Thinking ]
Oh, I can't believe I have to

00:07:05.191 --> 00:07:07.526
pretend to laugh at this crap.

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:09.561
Give me a break, man.

00:07:09.561 --> 00:07:11.964
-Next up, this one says...

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.202
The next one says...

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:20.840
-[ Thinking ]
Eh, already got a Grammy,

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:25.010
but I'm about to win an Oscar
for this laughing.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:27.280
-Here's another one.
This one says...

00:07:30.949 --> 00:07:33.219
Next up, this one says...

00:07:35.921 --> 00:07:40.025
[ Thinking ] Oh, man.

00:07:40.025 --> 00:07:44.563
This is the funniest [bleep]
we've ever done.

00:07:44.563 --> 00:07:46.599
[ Laughs ]

00:07:51.704 --> 00:07:56.142
-And finally...
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God!

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:01.480
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:04.583
-Glad you guys all enjoyed that.

00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:08.420
-Oh! Oh!

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.656
[ Laughs ]

00:08:10.656 --> 00:08:11.690
Whew!

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:13.592
-And, finally,
this made me laugh.

00:08:13.592 --> 00:08:16.462
Facebook made an error
and removed the official page

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:20.299
for the French town
Ville de Bitche.

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:23.035
The error is being blamed on
a censoring algorithm,

00:08:23.035 --> 00:08:25.537
but a prime suspect is
a Facebook employee from

00:08:25.537 --> 00:08:28.006
the neighboring town,
Hole d'Arse.

00:08:28.006 --> 00:08:29.041
We have a great show.

